<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zayyan ibn Mardanish</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zayyan ibn Mardanish was the last Muslim ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a>, a descendant of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-mardanish">Muhammad ibn Mardanish</a>, the Wolf King. In 1229 he overthrew the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad</a> governor Abu Zayd and took Valencia, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-i-of-aragon">James I of Aragon</a> conquered the kingdom, winning at Puig in 1237 and taking the city after a siege in 1238. Zayyan then withdrew to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murcia">Murcia</a> and later to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>.</p></div>
